# Test: operation correlation IDs (`| operation <id>`), bounded reload history (`show system reload history`), reload status (`show system reload status`), and always-on daemon liveness watchdog (`show system watchdog`) work end-to-end on a live daemon.
# QUESTION: on a live `ze start` daemon, does `show system watchdog` report `running: true` with `ticks > 0` and healthy probes (`config-tx-lock`, `command-handlers`), do `show system triage`, `show system reload status`, and `show system reload history` record both applied and rejected reloads with distinct generations and `operation-id`, do `show audit | operation <id>`, `show log recent | operation <id>`, and `show system reload history | operation <id>` return correlated records for that exact reload `operation-id`, and are `doctor-command-handler-hung` and `doctor-daemon-stall-detected` explainable via `ze show diagnostic`?
# A unit test cannot decide this because the path spans live `cmd/ze/hub` startup (`watchdog.Start()`), SSH CLI command dispatch, disk audit store persistence, real `request reload` execution across valid and refused configurations, `slogutil.LogRing` context extraction, and CLI `| operation <id>` pipe parsing end-to-end.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-ai-diagnostics-4-correlation-and-wedge-survival AC-7, AC-8.
# PREVENTS: missing watchdog startup in `cmd/ze/hub/main.go`, broken reload history or `operation-id` correlation across live audit/log/reload-history surfaces, or missing doctor diagnostic code registrations.

